    <listOfParameters>
      <parameter id="PODOSE_ethanol" name="oral ethanol dose [mg]" value="0" units="mg" constant="false"/>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="F_czx_abs" name="fraction absorbed chlorzoxazone" value="1" units="dimensionless" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p>Fraction of the chlorzoxazone in the intestinal lumen which is absorbed,
<code>(1 - F_czx_abs)</code> is excreted in the feces. Chlorzoxazone is absorbed
completely: 71-74 % of an oral dose are recovered as
6-hydroxychlorzoxazone in the urine (Desiraju1983, Kharasch1993), the
rest is a second, unidentified elimination of chlorzoxazone (see
<code>CZXOTHER</code> of the liver), not a fecal loss.</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
      </parameter>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="Ka_abs_czx" name="absorption rate chlorzoxazone" value="1.17342368845129" units="per_hr" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p>Rate of absorption from the intestinal lumen. Solutions peak at about
0.5 hr (Hohmann2019, Witt2016), Desiraju1983 report an absorption rate
of 2.28 1/hr after 750 mg in solution, Leclercq1998 2.0 1/hr after a
capsule.</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
